      "dom_id": "question-49530",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $u=x+3$, which integral is equivalent to $\\int x\\sqrt[4]{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $u=x+3$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=u-3.$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt[4]{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (u-3)(\\sqrt[4]{u})(\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int (u-3)({u}^{1/4})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int ({u}^{5/4}-3{u}^{1/4})\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
